{"t": 1793693349.42, "kind": "model_text", "turn": 8, "text": "Lab report:\n\nMeasured 5 pendulums, all reliable:\n- E1 0.39 m: T0 1.24598 +/-0.00051 s, 11.1 deg, 16.3 cycles, fit vs crossings 0.48 sigma. No warnings.\n- E2 0.619 +/-0.003 m: T0 1.58521 +/-0.00075 s, 11.5 deg, 12.3 cycles, fit vs crossings 0.23 sigma. Warning 2 outlier frames removed; still reliable.\n- E3 0.2887 +/-0.003 m: T0 1.08676 +/-0.00019 s, 19.1 deg, 31.1 cycles, fit vs crossings 0.61 sigma. No warnings.\n- E4 0.489 +/-0.003 m: T0 1.39817 +/-0.00026 s, 7.0 deg, 23.2 cycles, fit vs crossings 0.14 sigma. No warnings.\n- E5 0.697 +/-0.003 m: T0 1.66505 +/-0.00038 s, 8.3 deg, 16.3 cycles, fit vs crossings 0.24 sigma. No warnings.\n\nDamping AIC:\n- E5: quadratic best (weight 0.774), viscous delta 2.46 behind, coulomb delta 15.35, undamped delta 1555.06. Quadratic preferred, not decisive over viscous.\n- E4: viscous best (weight 0.949), coulomb delta 6.01, quadratic delta 10.7, undamped delta 1792.1. Viscous preferred over coulomb.\n- E2: quadratic best (weight 0.722), viscous delta 2.1, coulomb delta 6.72, undamped delta 704.82. Quadratic preferred, not decisive.\nNo single law wins everywhere. Undamped has essentially no support. Period is identical across models to ~0.00001 s, so g is unaffected.\n\ng fit with length offset from E1,E2,E3,E4,E5: g 10.0028 +/-0.0967 m/s2, offset 0.0098 +/-0.0053 m, chi2 10.57 for 3 dof.\n\nVerification P4 vs E5, blind true, length mismatch 0.43%: predicted T0 1.67699 +/-0.0055 s at 0.697 m, measured T0 1.66505 +/-0.00038 s, difference -0.71251%, z -2.16814, verdict tension.\n\nNew prediction P5 for 0.55 m at 10.0 deg: T0 1.4864 +/-0.00447 s, period at amplitude 1.48923 +/-0.00448 s. Request sent for 0.55 m golf-ball/thread test.\n\nNext step: record the 0.55 m experiment to test P5 interpolation between 0.489 m and 0.619 m.\n"}
